Panel init stream during the card read.

The SPL powers the panel before the logo read (every model), and once the
vendor reset steps are done it sends the panel's init stream (GPIO SPI on
PI8-PI10) between card reads, honouring every vendor delay as a minimum.
It records where it stopped in the panel record (version 2). The helper
checks that record and carries on: the rest of the stream, then the
vendor's 50 ms, TCON enable, 100 ms and backlight, as before. If the record
is missing or does not add up, the helper resets the panel and sends the
whole stream itself, as E1 does when the SPL did not power the panel.

